for power, vampires wielding sex as weapon, vampires keeping harems of slaved humans, and so on.<br /> <br /> It's nothing to be afraid of.<br /> <br /> It's part of the vampire experience and a weapon as well as motivation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T16:17:25-07:00","id":1514775,"title":"","content":"The success of the Anne Rice Interview show probably motivates this one,I'm optimistic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T16:57:04-07:00","id":1514780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1514727#post1514727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026<br /> <br /> On a different note: Tiktok?? How is <i>Tiktok</i> an &quot;alternative play technique&quot;? What does that even mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a whole bunch of people who TikTok LARP, in the fact they dress up as characters and lip synch movie quotes and song lyrics. The screen grab I saw on the write up of TikTok essentially describes a thing people have been doing on the clock app for a few years now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T17:22:28-07:00","id":1514781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1514772#post1514772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I do adult R-Rated vampire games where sex is just part of the storytelling. Vampires seducing people for power, vampires wielding sex as weapon, vampires keeping harems of slaved humans, and so on.<br /> <br /> It's nothing to be afraid of.<br /> <br /> It's part of the vampire experience and a weapon as well as motivation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is contesting that this shouldn't be a topic for VtM to talk about. The question is why we're seeing this now, with so much other stuff not covered, and what the specific hints as to what the book will cover will really do to help bring this into play in a fashion that's good for multiple approaches (and with far more taste than V5 core has in an infamous line).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T06:20:43-07:00","id":1514838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1514780#post1514780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are a whole bunch of people who TikTok LARP, in the fact they dress up as characters and lip synch movie quotes and song lyrics. The screen grab I saw on the write up of TikTok essentially describes a thing people have been doing on the clock app for a few years now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, which is yet another topic that's already been covered. There's more than enough on the topic in the V5 Players Guide (in my opinion the whole section on online-play could've been shorter overall). Especially because by referring to online-entities like specific social media the whole thing is in danger of becoming outdated pretty fast in the future. I think that sort of content/advice would be better served as a blog-post on the WOD-website instead of &quot;setting it in stone&quot; so-to-speak by dedicating a section of a book to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T10:51:11-07:00","id":1514860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1514781#post1514781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think anyone is contesting that this shouldn't be a topic for VtM to talk about. The question is why we're seeing this now, with so much other stuff not covered, and what the specific hints as to what the book will cover will really do to help bring this into play in a fashion that's good for multiple approaches (and with far more taste than V5 core has in an infamous line).</div> </div> </div> </div>My theory is because Renegade and Paradox are allergic to lore. This is not completely a criticism but they seem to have no interest in doing anything but a surface interaction with the world building and mostly doing tool-kits.<br /> <br /> So, as far as they're concerned, it's done now that they've done Anarchs, Camarilla, Sabbat, and Inquisition.<br /> <br /> And now it's time for storytelling tips.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T12:42:10-07:00","id":1514873,"title":"","content":"OK? But let's look at the relatively similarly lore-agnostic VtR 1e and just how many books that covered more niche topics there really were to deal with (yes some of these are partially covered in some V5 supplements, but none in detail despite older books dedicated to these topics):<br /> <br /> Expansion on how to run coteries, different types, what happens as character goals drift over time, etc.<br /> How do Kindred that decide to travel extensively manage (and this is definitely still a thing in V5)<br /> Ghouls (though probably also any expanded Thin-Blood stuff as they ate up a lot of narrative space of things like Revenants).<br /> City building and how to run vampires controlling mortal institutions<br /> Stranger antagonists than other vampires and hunters<br /> Social influence as a tool of control<br /> How to handle scaling up the stakes of the game beyond local matters<br /> Guide to homebrewing Discipline powers, Amlgams, Rituals, etic.<br /> <br /> All of those fall into the &quot;tool-kit, not world building,&quot; kind of things. And I'm pretty sure most of those are more useful topics to get to before we get into more details on vampire sex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T15:51:00-07:00","id":1514890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1514860#post1514860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026So, as far as they're concerned, it's done now that they've done Anarchs, Camarilla, Sabbat, and Inquisition.<br /> <br /> And now it's time for storytelling tips.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>With how much the Camarilla book talked about the Ashirra without actually saying anything about them there\u2019s room to add some fresh lore to the game and give it something prior editions didn\u2019t really touch.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T23:03:28-07:00","id":1514920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1514890#post1514890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With how much the Camarilla book talked about the Ashirra without actually saying anything about them there\u2019s room to add some fresh lore to the game and give it something prior editions didn\u2019t really touch.</div> </div> </div> </div>That writer is definitely still there in the WOD-team because there was one particular writer that you always could immediately pick out in the V5 Players Guide. And the way you would notice it is that whenever this particular writer talked about the Sects in V5, he never talked about Anarchs, Camarilla and Sabbat, instead that writer would focus on the Anarchs, Camarilla and Ashirra in the descriptions.<br /> <br /> Whoever that is certainly would be in favor of a supplement on the Ashirra, I would think... but he's in the WOD-team and the supplements are done by Renegade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T01:18:36-07:00","id":1514926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1514360#post1514360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since it's most likely to be a necromancy ceremony, and necromancy is usually associated with death and the dead, I hypothesize that it has something to do with Romeo and Juliet.<br /> <br /> Weak reasoning, I know.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Orpheus and Eurydice, surely? Given the Giovanni's core sphere of influence, it has to be.<br /> <br /> Inanna and Dumuzid, being related to Ishtar, would be more of a Toreador thing, as would the Aphrodite and Adonis version.<br /> <br /> Romeo &amp; Juliet seems a bit too quaint for the Kindred. Though, I guess there's a sort of perverse analogue to the story already in Moloch and Troile. Now that I'd read more about! But I doubt it because of V5's aversion to that sort of historic fluff (and the Baali don't exist much/at all in V5).<br /> <br /> In fact, though I can't see V5 plumbing these kinds of mythological links much (as the devs seem to see it as a distraction from present-day, street-level play), the Hecata name is the glaring exception. If there's an Oblivion ceremony, then maybe they will draw on some of that.<br /> <br /> But if I had to hazard a guess, I'd say we'll get more rules on vampire sex, then loads of essays on romance and intimacy in games, possible with a teensy bit of lore about the Vermilion Wedding. We might also get some stuff on Touchstones as the obvious mechanical aspect here, and maybe a few new Loresheets.<br /> <br /> My guess is that it'll be 60% RP advice, 30% fluff and 10% mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 06-14-2023, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T06:33:07-07:00","id":1514952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1514920#post1514920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That writer is definitely still there in the WOD-team because there was one particular writer that you always could immediately pick out in the V5 Players Guide. And the way you would notice it is that whenever this particular writer talked about the Sects in V5, he never talked about Anarchs, Camarilla and Sabbat, instead that writer would focus on the Anarchs, Camarilla and Ashirra in the descriptions.<br /> <br /> Whoever that is certainly would be in favor of a supplement on the Ashirra, I would think... but he's in the WOD-team and the supplements are done by Renegade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Karim is the only person listed as a writer in the Camarilla book, everyone else would be considered a freelancer for the Players Guide. I don\u2019t have the PG to compare writing credits, but it makes sense to exclude the Sabbat when talking about sects since they\u2019re supposed to be antagonists only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T12:06:34-07:00","id":1514995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1514952#post1514952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Karim is the only person listed as a writer in the Camarilla book, everyone else would be considered a freelancer for the Players Guide. I don\u2019t have the PG to compare writing credits, but it makes sense to exclude the Sabbat when talking about sects since they\u2019re supposed to be antagonists only.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Sabbat not being a player-option, the Ashirra certainly would be an actually interesting area to explore in the V5-setting. That certainly would interest me more than a supplement about vampire romance and sex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T11:47:25-07:00","id":1515169,"title":"","content":"All I can do is laugh at the stupidity of this. This is what we get a sourcebook on? Not a follow up to Beckett's Jyhad Diary? No source book detailing the Gehenna War? Not another city book?<br /> Can a competent tabletop publisher pick up the IP soon? Paradox has to be driving it's value down.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T12:03:17-07:00","id":1515170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515169#post1515169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I can do is laugh at the stupidity of this. This is what we get a sourcebook on? Not a follow up to Beckett's Jyhad Diary? No source book detailing the Gehenna War? Not another city book?<br /> Can a competent tabletop publisher pick up the IP soon? Paradox has to be driving it's value down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires have been tied to romance for a.long time, the most successful vampire show currently airing is a Anne Rice show after all,the idea might not be of your liking but its not stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T13:32:46-07:00","id":1515175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1514995#post1514995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With Sabbat not being a player-option, the Ashirra certainly would be an actually interesting area to explore in the V5-setting. That certainly would interest me more than a supplement about vampire romance and sex.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really expect them to do anything with the Ashirra beyond just a few mentions, as they've already been doing now. If they can't even stomach the Sabbat to the point where they relegated them as antagonist-only NPCs, the Ashirra will be even harder to write due to the fact they're heavily tied to Islam as a Sect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T19:18:32-07:00","id":1515198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515175#post1515175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really expect them to do anything with the Ashirra beyond just a few mentions, as they've already been doing now. If they can't even stomach the Sabbat to the point where they relegated them as antagonist-only NPCs, the Ashirra will be even harder to write due to the fact they're heavily tied to Islam as a Sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've stated that their intent is the Ashirra and Camarilla are now one sect.<br /> <br /> The Vermillion Wedding turns out to have been a full corporate merger.<br /> <br /> But they're SO uninterested in lore, they couldn't bother to explain that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T19:47:54-07:00","id":1515200,"title":"","content":"I actually find it bizarre that Parawolf even remembered the Ashirra was even a thing in VtM, but I guess for all practical purposes I think it's been relegated to the common Hecata/Loresheet strategy of V5; consolidate a niche, but interesting tidbit and put into a more mainstream-ish / quick to stomach part of the setting and just call it a day. <br /> <br /> With the Ashirra merged with the Camarilla now apparently, what happens to the 7 Salubri who were a part of that Sect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T22:55:11-07:00","id":1515206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515169#post1515169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I can do is laugh at the stupidity of this. This is what we get a sourcebook on? Not a follow up to Beckett's Jyhad Diary? No source book detailing the Gehenna War? Not another city book?<br /> Can a competent tabletop publisher pick up the IP soon? Paradox has to be driving it's value down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deep down in my dark little heart I secretly hoped they scrap V5 and <i>Vampire</i>: The Masquerade \u2013 30th Anniversary Edition will come out, basically to follow where Beckett's Jyhad Diary ended...<br /> Still not gave up on <i>Vampire</i>: The Masquerade \u2013 40th Anniversary Edition tho'! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But asaide my personal taste and cold enmity I have against V5 (or any [insert game line]5 for that mater under the aegis of Paradox...) I could accept a middle ground with a detailed Gehenna War book or Beckett's Jyhad Diary Volume II.<br /> On the other hand I'm terrified what they would do with them... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Not having them is actually better; what they don't touch they can't ruin<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515170#post1515170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires have been tied to romance for a.long time, the most successful vampire show currently airing is a Anne Rice show after all,the idea might not be of your liking but its not stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tastes differ<br /> But I think the vampire genre stil lrecovering form the Twilight era...<br /> And lets not forget, Dracula is a horror novel, but it's also a novel which deals with the theme of love in various ways.The novel itself is not romantic, but romantic love is a key part of various relationships in the novel.<br /> I'm not sure we need a source book on this (especially not one with the usual gloom, doom, you are not allowed to love... ever and you are cursed to ruin your relationship)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515200#post1515200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Ashirra merged with the Camarilla now apparently, what happens to the 7 Salubri who were a part of that Sect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Merg is a very strong word<br /> The Ashirra and the Camarilla have formed<i> an alliance</i>, symbolically represented by the Vermilion Wedding of Victoria Ash and Tegyrius as a sign of trust between the two sects.<br /> The Ashirra have protected seven al-Amin from destruction into the Final Nights thanks to an accord between the Old Man of the Mountain and the Salubri methuselah Nahum ben Enosh. They are protected as long as they live in Ashirra territory and their numbers never surpass seven. The seven are treated as royalty, but are always watched...<br /> I don't think this changed/will change<br /> If you are an al-Amin, you are safe as long as you remain in Ashirra territory (I highly doubt the Ashirra after the Alliance would consider the Camarilla territory Ashirra territory or vica versa) - leave and you are... well... Tremere are not around (nor the Baali in V5) so probably nothing serious would happen<br /> Logically, as an al-Amin is a honored guest of the Ashirra core member even, the Camarilla to avoid some diplomatic issues, would be quick to make sure the al-Amin are protected too - like a celebrity or an ambassador or a royalty of a foregin country when not at home.<br /> Actually those are nice story hooks - the coterie is tasked by the Prince or even the inner circle to make sure the visiting precious unicorn is not harmed (sush, don't mention <i>our</i> Salubri runing around in our cities)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T00:29:08-07:00","id":1515214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515169#post1515169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I can do is laugh at the stupidity of this. This is what we get a sourcebook on? Not a follow up to Beckett's Jyhad Diary? No source book detailing the Gehenna War? Not another city book?<br /> Can a competent tabletop publisher pick up the IP soon? Paradox has to be driving it's value down.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don\u2019t care about that stuff, they just want to make Generic Vampire Game, but couldn\u2019t be bothered starting their own and risking not being popular, so instead they buy someone elses, pay just enough lip-service to establish being in the same universe, then get right down to making Generic Vampire Game sourcebooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T01:59:56-07:00","id":1515218,"title":"","content":"So, I should be in the target group for a book like this. I like books that talk about how to integrate romance, relationships, sex, and eroticism into a game (without it becoming a cringe fest), I also have done solo plays where sexuality and even NSFW content played an important part.<br /> <br /> However, I feel there are so many topics that should be covered before that... such as how to handle elders (because despite telling us the Beckoning is getting to all of them, there are still plenty elders around), city building (Damnation City for V5), V5 updates for Guilded Cage and Midnight Siege, a new city book, a book of suggestions on how to play V5 in other eras, hell, even a V5 update of Children of the Night, etc. All of them would be more immediately useful to most tables.<br /> <br /> Add to that that I wasn't a fan of the past few books, despite loving V5 in general (and as someone who's playing VtM since 1993), so I'm extremely skeptical whether this book is the right move at the right time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T02:01:52-07:00","id":1515219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caerolion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515214#post1515214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don\u2019t care about that stuff, they just want to make Generic Vampire Game, but couldn\u2019t be bothered starting their own and risking not being popular, so instead they buy someone elses, pay just enough lip-service to establish being in the same universe, then get right down to making Generic Vampire Game sourcebooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a bit unfair to them, even if I am deeply unhappy with most of the decisions they made. I think V5 came from a position of great love for the game. They just had love for one specific subtype of Vampire games and felt that the other elements and game subtypes were deterimental to their vision of Vampire. In their decision to pursue this vision at expense of everything else we ended up with v5 in this strange state it is.<br /> <br /> And I don't mind there being a romance book for vampire, it's a genre staple. I'd just like to see other elements fleshed out and I have zero faith in them treating the topic with forethought and tact it requires.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T02:12:08-07:00","id":1515221,"title":"","content":"While I'm curious about what on earth the Beckoning and the Gehenna war involve exactly, because it sounds like an interesting Chronicle, if a terrible metaplot choice, I find myself agreeing with this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515206#post1515206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand I'm terrified what they would do with them... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Not having them is actually better; what they don't touch they can't ruin</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ruined&quot; is only an opinion, not an objective thing, but I just... personally, I <i>don't</i> want to know. I've already seen what's been done to the Sabbat and the Garou, and even the stuff I didn't consider mangled beyond recovery felt, at best, unsatisfying/incomplete. If V5 wants to make a hundred supplements about the vampire romance genre (or even using V5 in different genres common to vampires. Like focus on horror specifically, or religious horror or whatever) I would find that preferable at this stage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-16-2023, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T02:55:27-07:00","id":1515222,"title":"","content":"I guess my thoughts are largely, &quot;whatever.&quot; It's not a subject that I find very appealing, but then I've been playing for a pretty long time. It might be useful for newer STs because dealing with romance at the table can be really difficult and awkward when you don't know what you're doing.<br /> <br /> I think there are other subjects that would be better to cover in the books, but if Renegade thinks this will bring in more money than those other things, good luck to them.<br /> <br /> Ultimately my takeaway is that they don't really want to do VtM like a typical RPG or have a publication order like you'd normally see. They want to do things differently to make the game stand out I guess. I don't think that's a great idea but oh well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-16-2023, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T03:14:19-07:00","id":1515223,"title":"","content":"They're probably going to have to build some additional mechanics if they want to do this in relation to hunger. Its already pretty fucked up what happens if you get messy crit on seduction rolls it'll be outright unworkable in a long term romance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T03:48:30-07:00","id":1515225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515223#post1515223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're probably going to have to build some additional mechanics if they want to do this in relation to hunger. Its already pretty fucked up what happens if you get messy crit on seduction rolls it'll be outright unworkable in a long term romance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha, I'd be surprised if they addressed it at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T06:21:59-07:00","id":1515235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515218#post1515218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... such as how to handle elders (because despite telling us the Beckoning is getting to all of them, there are still plenty elders around), city building (Damnation City for V5), V5 updates for Guilded Cage and Midnight Siege, a new city book, a book of suggestions on how to play V5 in other eras, hell, even a V5 update of Children of the Night, etc. All of them would be more immediately useful to most tables...</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here. With the attempted focus on the coterie, books about how cities function and the place the coteries fit in the picture would go a long way to reinforcing it. You want to give me a sense on what threats kindred face in V5 and how to deal with them? Update Midnight Siege to include Second Inquisition tactics, ways conflicts play out when Anarchs press to takeover a city and vice versa, etc. Show me how the V5 setting is different instead of relying on \u201clegacy\u201d products for information.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T06:27:04-07:00","id":1515236,"title":"","content":"The reason why they've gone to lengths to include the Ashirra is... because they want to appear inclusive. <br /> Do they actually care about muslims? Not at all. It's a really weird gesture to give muslims a group of vampires that do Haram things but still insist they're an islamic sect. Imagine trying to promote veganism by colouring your steaks green. There's a context where the Ashirra make sense but it's not in modern nights, especially when real world politics is such a mess and the middle east was a lot less religious 100 years ago. Would your average Iranian appreciate the concept that their vampires are better and more enlightened because they're more perversely religious? No. <br /> <br /> It's the same story as them hiring that cultural advisor who spoke out: they don't actually give a shit, they just want to look like they do. <br /> <br /> Which brings me to the upcomming Romance book... <br /> I think it'll just be lots of ill-conceived queer things. Like they'll go out of their way to include non-mainstream stuff, and maybe actually make LGTBQ stuff look worse because, y'know, vampires are doing it, and bad writing of course. If you don't like it, you're a bigot and can't appreciate a company pretending to care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T07:19:28-07:00","id":1515240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515170#post1515170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires have been tied to romance for a.long time, the most successful vampire show currently airing is a Anne Rice show after all,the idea might not be of your liking but its not stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point. There is so much inspiration for it already, the idea of a sourcebook on something so generic is ridiculous. We don't need a romance vampire sourcebook. We have the rules for blood bonds, we've seen or read interview with a vampire, True Blood and the series it is based on is out there. The majority of my characters have been in relationships with NPCs, I didn\u2019t need a sourcebook to tell me how.<br /> <br /> Not to mention vampire are not exactly subtle metaphors for violation and sexual assault. But lets devote a whole sourcebook to &quot;vampire romance&quot; instead of something actually relevant to the gameline. We are what, like 5 years into V5's release cycle and we still don't know what the beckoning actually is! And don't give me &quot;it's whatever the gm wants it to be&quot;. If i wanted that I'd play Requiem. People play masquerade for the setting and Paradox continues to actively mismanage it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T10:55:02-07:00","id":1515265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515240#post1515240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the point. There is so much inspiration for it already, the idea of a sourcebook on something so generic is ridiculous. We don't need a romance vampire sourcebook. We have the rules for blood bonds, we've seen or read interview with a vampire, True Blood and the series it is based on is out there. The majority of my characters have been in relationships with NPCs, I didn\u2019t need a sourcebook to tell me how.<br /> <br /> Not to mention vampire are not exactly subtle metaphors for violation and sexual assault. But lets devote a whole sourcebook to &quot;vampire romance&quot; instead of something actually relevant to the gameline. We are what, like 5 years into V5's release cycle and we still don't know what the beckoning actually is! And don't give me &quot;it's whatever the gm wants it to be&quot;. If i wanted that I'd play Requiem. People play masquerade for the setting and Paradox continues to actively mismanage it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The beckoning isn't a call from the third generation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T11:58:23-07:00","id":1515278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515200#post1515200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually find it bizarre that Parawolf even remembered the Ashirra was even a thing in VtM, but I guess for all practical purposes I think it's been relegated to the common Hecata/Loresheet strategy of V5; consolidate a niche, but interesting tidbit and put into a more mainstream-ish / quick to stomach part of the setting and just call it a day.<br /> <br /> With the Ashirra merged with the Camarilla now apparently, what happens to the 7 Salubri who were a part of that Sect?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Salubri are notably back to being in a main book and in the Vamprie Players Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T12:07:13-07:00","id":1515281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515236#post1515236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why they've gone to lengths to include the Ashirra is... because they want to appear inclusive.<br /> Do they actually care about muslims? Not at all. It's a really weird gesture to give muslims a group of vampires that do Haram things but still insist they're an islamic sect. Imagine trying to promote veganism by colouring your steaks green. There's a context where the Ashirra make sense but it's not in modern nights, especially when real world politics is such a mess and the middle east was a lot less religious 100 years ago. Would your average Iranian appreciate the concept that their vampires are better and more enlightened because they're more perversely religious? No.<br /> <br /> It's the same story as them hiring that cultural advisor who spoke out: they don't actually give a shit, they just want to look like they do.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to the upcomming Romance book...<br /> I think it'll just be lots of ill-conceived queer things. Like they'll go out of their way to include non-mainstream stuff, and maybe actually make LGTBQ stuff look worse because, y'know, vampires are doing it, and bad writing of course. If you don't like it, you're a bigot and can't appreciate a company pretending to care.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a><br /> <br /> That feels like it actually makes the point of the Paradox take on the Ashirra. Yes, the Ashirra do a lot of forbidden things. But so do all of the Christian Noddist vampires. It's why the mental gymnastics they do to justify themselves fall flat. It's probably why they had no difficulty merging with the Camarilla in the Modern Nights.<br /> <br /> But rather than &quot;inclusive&quot;, I'd argue that a better way of phrasing it is that Paradox realizes 60-90% of the people who still play Vampire are actually in other countries than America now.<br /> <br /> Including them.<br /> <br /> So they want The Camarilla to be a global worldwide vampire conspiracy, which was how it was in 1st Edition. It's also probably why the Kuei-Jin were retconned out of existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-16-2023, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T13:17:45-07:00","id":1515294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515236#post1515236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why they've gone to lengths to include the Ashirra is... because they want to appear inclusive.<br /> Do they actually care about muslims? Not at all. It's a really weird gesture to give muslims a group of vampires that do Haram things but still insist they're an islamic sect.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be completly fair none of the major religions are going to be pro vampire so some sort of accommodation is needed unless you're going full heresy/haram.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T13:40:27-07:00","id":1515297,"title":"","content":"Nah. <br /> The Sabbat mocks and is directly antagonistic towards the Catholic faith. Worshipping the first murderer? They might as well praise lucifer, build babel and seek to make a new Sodom and Gamorah. While there might be some pockets of exceptions, they spit in the face of abrahamic faith.<br /> <br /> Other noddists, at best, simply aren't invested in abraham. They have the reasonable argument that the descendants of caine were meant to be different from the descendents of seth (and Abel if he had any descendents; I don't believe it's known who Noah and his son's married since women weren't worthy of much detail then) <br /> <br /> The Ashirra on the other hand apparently have the sincere belief that they're good Muslims, even though they drink blood (Haram) are hurt by faith (take that as a sign) and pray at night (just wrong) and a whole bunch of other mental gymnastics. . Most Noddists have the good sense to divorce themselves from Abraham's folk, Moses doesn't register to them, never mind Jesus. But the Ashirra as written insists it's following Mohammed's teachings.. which is just... there's no argument for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T14:16:57-07:00","id":1515300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515297#post1515297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah.<br /> The Sabbat mocks and is directly antagonistic towards the Catholic faith. Worshipping the first murderer? They might as well praise lucifer, build babel and seek to make a new Sodom and Gamorah. While there might be some pockets of exceptions, they spit in the face of abrahamic faith.<br /> <br /> Other noddists, at best, simply aren't invested in abraham. They have the reasonable argument that the descendants of caine were meant to be different from the descendents of seth (and Abel if he had any descendents; I don't believe it's known who Noah and his son's married since women weren't worthy of much detail then)<br /> <br /> The Ashirra on the other hand apparently have the sincere belief that they're good Muslims, even though they drink blood (Haram) are hurt by faith (take that as a sign) and pray at night (just wrong) and a whole bunch of other mental gymnastics. . Most Noddists have the good sense to divorce themselves from Abraham's folk, Moses doesn't register to them, never mind Jesus. But the Ashirra as written insists it's following Mohammed's teachings.. which is just... there's no argument for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat aren't real Noddists anymore than the Westboro Baptist Church is to Christianity.<br /> <br /> 1st Edition made it clear that the Camarilla's culture is Noddist to the core and the whole &quot;The Camarilla denies the Antediluvians&quot; business was just bullshit Hardelstadt was obsessed with but the moment he was dead, everyone broke out their copies of the Book of Nod. And before you say THAT'S the Retcon, I remind you that the Clan Books of the Ventrue, Generation, and plenty of other sources are steeped in Noddism.<br /> <br /> But I think you're wrong about the Ashirra.<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> <br /> Because the Ashirra have NEVER been sincere about their Islamic faith. Even in the original Dark Age books, they had a bunch of Pagan Methuselah members and Atheist assholes.<br /> <br /> The &quot;We're all Muslim Vampires&quot; business was just a cover for their power games with a conveinant way of manipulating vampires born in the past few centuries. They even underscore this in the one decent part of THE CAMARILLA where a British Muslim vampire visits the Ashirra and gets the cold shoulder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-16-2023, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T14:18:08-07:00","id":1515301,"title":"","content":"Whose laws do the follow? <br /> <br /> Noddists<br /> Caine. Only Caine. Maybe there's some others in there but it can be assured all the authors are vampires. God's the antagonist, Lilith's a bitch, the children of seth are your opposition and you should not be beholden to their laws. Noah, Moses, Abraham, Jacob, Jesus, Mohammed... these people are completely irrelevant to vampires, you might as well be discussing the laws of Svartalfheim.<br /> <br /> The Ashirra<br /> God, ten commandments, Mohammed and his apostles, all the extra laws agreed upon by Muslims but someone did some modifications for convenience and yet the prophet certainly wouldn't approve of such things...<br /> <br /> <br /> Completely different animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T14:21:11-07:00","id":1515302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515301#post1515301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whose laws do the follow?<br /> <br /> Noddists<br /> Caine. Only Caine. Maybe there's some others in there but it can be assured all the authors are vampires. God's the antagonist, Lilith's a bitch, the children of seth are your opposition and you should not be beholden to their laws. Noah, Moses, Abraham, Jacob, Jesus, Mohammed... these people are completely irrelevant to vampires, you might as well be discussing the laws of Svartalfheim.<br /> <br /> The Ashirra<br /> God, ten commandments, Mohammed and his apostles, all the extra laws agreed upon by Muslims but someone did some modifications for convenience and yet the prophet certainly wouldn't approve of such things...<br /> <br /> <br /> Completely different animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Ashirra isn't remotely sincere about it's Islam.<br /> <br /> And there's no difference above because both are fundamentally just lies about saying vampires are God's Chosen. Which they aren't.<br /> <br /> Neither acknowledges vampires are the Damned.<br /> <br /> Which, in that respect, the Sabbat are correct.<br /> <br /> Also, why do you keep bringing up the &quot;blood drinking&quot; element? Is that really a bigger deal than being a living corpse burned by faith?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T04:36:42-07:00","id":1515343,"title":"","content":"Being Ashirra is one of the perfectly reasonable religious rationalizations of Undeath. <br /> <br /> Ashirra and many old practitioners of the Road of Heaven thought of themselves as Monsters, but that could be saved through Jesus's sacrifice or Muhammad's revelaton<br /> <br /> <br /> Others practitioners of the Road of Heaven, up to the extremes of the Cainite Heresy and Church of Caine, spoke of being Chosen by God. An opposite variant of this line of thought is the Path of Night and Path of Cathari, vampires as God's Ordained Evil. <br /> <br /> Then, there is Vampires as Damned Rebels, from the Sabbat to Infernalism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T05:36:03-07:00","id":1515353,"title":"","content":"Coming up with whole new rules or interpretations of religious texts that are absolute blasphemy to the others - as well as outright just doing Olympian feats of mental gymnastics to explain why the power/s that be are totally cool with whatever horrible thing you/your in-group are doing - and even genuinely believing in it, is a longstanding human tradition; I don't think it's that hard to believe that vampires would come up with their own vampire-specific sects like the Ashirra (which google translate suggests is more like &quot;eushayra\u200b&quot; or something) where being a vampire is divinely ordained/a-ok. The fact that it would likely be very offensive to most, if not all other, sects of their faith is irrelevant (and probably the point, from the writer's point of view &quot;vampires are an unholy mockery of humanity that defile everything they touch, blah blah blah.&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T09:26:10-07:00","id":1515378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515302#post1515302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, why do you keep bringing up the &quot;blood drinking&quot; element? Is that really a bigger deal than being a living corpse burned by faith?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because - I guess - there is a conflict there between religion and basic food drive when it comes to the Ashirra<br /> In theory, human blood should be &quot;Haram&quot; aka. any act that is forbidden by Allah; one of the five Islamic commandments - Foods which are not considered halal for Muslims to consume include blood<br /> While to be a living corpse burned by faith is not against any of the Islamic commandments and in some cases viewed by the Will of Allah<br /> Salat - the Five Daily Prayers are doable, tho' requires a great deal of willpower - then again, the Ashirra are devoted (most of the time)<br /> BUT when it comes to Blood? At first glance problematic<br /> The vampires of the Ashirra have a really nice Halal ceremony to &quot;sanctify&quot; and purify the blood involving a silver bowl and prayer - devoted Ashirra members rarely <i>if ever</i> eat from a human!<br /> Of course there are grey areas in this, boiling down to personal interpretation and preference, but what you said:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515302#post1515302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except the Ashirra isn't remotely sincere about it's Islam.</div> </div> </div> </div>is not <i>entirely</i> true, quite the opposite!<br /> <br /> The Sect is based on Faith and the members of the Ashirra genuinely believe that redemption for the Kindred was among the promises Muhammad made if they chose to follow Allah thus are the true followers of Islam... sure some of the Kindred involved in the Ashirra follow Islam because it is convenient for them, but still, <i>they follow it.</i><br /> <br /> Naturally, we don't really know whats happened between Veil of Night and V5, but considering Vampires are not famous of their ability to change and adapt in a short notice, the faith remained, especially when it was policed/supported by the Bay't Mutasharid, who - as every Nosferatu around that time - were deeply relegious and the Banu Haqim and in a sense, the al-Amin<br /> Also, don't forget Suleiman ibn Abdullah, was the founder and mullah of the Ashirra sect - rumored to have been a disciple of the Prophet Muhammad himself, so the Qabilat al-Khayal are very strong position in the relegion point of view (like the most of the LAsombra around that time)<br /> So I guess the Ashirra not really changed<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T14:27:37-07:00","id":1515417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515378#post1515378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is not <i>entirely</i> true, quite the opposite!<br /> <br /> The Sect is based on Faith and the members of the Ashirra genuinely believe that redemption for the Kindred was among the promises Muhammad made if they chose to follow Allah thus are the true followers of Islam... sure some of the Kindred involved in the Ashirra follow Islam because it is convenient for them, but still, <i>they follow it.</i><br /> <br /> Naturally, we don't really know whats happened between Veil of Night and V5, but considering Vampires are not famous of their ability to change and adapt in a short notice, the faith remained, especially when it was policed/supported by the Bay't Mutasharid, who - as every Nosferatu around that time - were deeply relegious and the Banu Haqim and in a sense, the al-Amin<br /> Also, don't forget Suleiman ibn Abdullah, was the founder and mullah of the Ashirra sect - rumored to have been a disciple of the Prophet Muhammad himself, so the Qabilat al-Khayal are very strong position in the relegion point of view (like the most of the LAsombra around that time)<br /> So I guess the Ashirra not really changed<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Except that ignores the large number of Elders who predated Islam and were giving lip service the entire time. I feel like those guys get ignored a lot.<br /> <br /> Also, the fact that as much as you want to believe the Ashirra are sincere, they also KNOW that approaching a Mosque with faithful members will burn them like fire.<br /> <br /> Which is to say they've ALWAYS been aware it is a bunch of mental headgames.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T15:11:14-07:00","id":1515422,"title":"","content":"Or we can just ignore any implication that Muslims in the Middle East are &quot;special&quot; and somehow are better at True Faith than everyone else (including Muslims in other parts of the world). The WoD has a very bad history of equating Islamic fundamentalists with related to Muslims in Muslim majority countries being so much more prone to extremism than it means that causes special effects in the Middle East (The Web of Faith, more True Faith, alternate rules for the Imbued, etc.). The whole creative origins of the Assamites set a tone of extremely biased takes on Muslim majority countries for decades of this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T16:07:55-07:00","id":1515426,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26836_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26836\" data-vbnamecard=\"26836\">Rhywbeth</a> I think it's that's a rational argument for humans as a whole but falls apart when it concerns exclusive and majority-educated groups like vampires. Tucker Carlson can grift his viewers with blatant bullshit but he's not going to fool another Tucker Carlson, the guy knows exactly what he's doing. There certainly are useful idiots out there that believe their own crap, but that's more 'ghoul' than vampire, y'know? <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a><br /> Elders pre-dating Islam aren't going to be very active and influential in modern nights. <br /> <br /> And if they're not actual believers, why bother the pretence in the first place? There's no benefit that outweighs the cons. It just comes across as smug and self-satisfied, and as Heavy Arms points out, an overcorrection of the racist muslim caricature that the assamites began as. I would go further and suggest a lot of it stems from poorly justified Iraq war guilt/ crusades guilt: ignorant western warmongers destroying enlightened muslim peace (The islamic golden age came at the direct expense of Christendom and Persia, but unfortunately history has once again made the mistake of not catering to modern sensibilities: blue eye men bad!) <br /> <br /> That, and yeah, i hold great objection to the implication that people in that part of the world get along better than others when, y'know.. no. History is not the europeans fighting among themselves while everyone else sang kumbayas. Petty wars for personal gain transcends culture. Its weird to imagine princes agreeing to a multinational binding when there's nothing for them to gain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T17:03:51-07:00","id":1515431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515426#post1515426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elders pre-dating Islam aren't going to be very active and influential in modern nights.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but they're going to be the people who were the actual powers behind the publicly Muslim Princes and potentates in the Ashirra. Given the Rise of the Shepards of Ur-Shulgi as well, we also get a sense that the Modern Nights Assamites were never as religious as peiople thought they were since half of them gladly renounced the Abrahamic God to worship an evil Blood God and wage war on their fellows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if they're not actual believers, why bother the pretence in the first place? There's no benefit that outweighs the cons. It just comes across as smug and self-satisfied, and as Heavy Arms points out, an overcorrection of the racist muslim caricature that the assamites began as. I would go further and suggest a lot of it stems from poorly justified Iraq war guilt/ crusades guilt: ignorant western warmongers destroying enlightened muslim peace (The islamic golden age came at the direct expense of Christendom and Persia, but unfortunately history has once again made the mistake of not catering to modern sensibilities: blue eye men bad!)<br /> <br /> That, and yeah, i hold great objection to the implication that people in that part of the world get along better than others when, y'know.. no. History is not the europeans fighting among themselves while everyone else sang kumbayas. Petty wars for personal gain transcends culture. Its weird to imagine princes agreeing to a multinational binding when there's nothing for them to gain. </div> </div> </div>It's a universal constant in the game line that any vampire culture will inherently be built on lies, backstabbing, power lust, and violence because of the Beast. The idea that the local vampires would make use of the prevailing religion to help control the younger undead makes perfect sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T22:38:05-07:00","id":1515444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1514355-renegade-game-studios-announce-blood-stained-love-a-romance-supplement-for-v5?p=1515417#post1515417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also, the fact that as much as you want to believe the Ashirra are sincere, they also KNOW that approaching a Mosque with faithful members will burn them like fire.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect, I think this is a hyperbole<br /> I humbly ask you to point where it is said, this is the case because I only remember Veil of Night where a Faith rating of a site is detailed - I could be wrong, thats why I ask<br /> It is true, if a site have a True Faith rating then it is very painfull (to the point even damages the vampire, maybe this is what you ment by burn them like fire?) to apporach the said site and stay there but not every site have a True Faith radiance - many do of course! The territory of the Ashirra is the part of the Web of Faith (but this means even as mortals it was natural to them to be faithful; a fact they probably carried in to their unlife)<br /> But there is the sirh Ritual <b>Allah's Blessing</b> ; it is allows a Cainite to <i>owercome</i> a place's True Faith even such a holy site's like Mecca nad Medina!<br /> The vampire is protected inside a holy place and make her stay &quot;comfortable&quot;<br /> <br /> And don't forget the <b>Keening, </b>a clamoring cacophony of wails and screams. The Keening manifests only during the day, but grows in intensity until it reaches its peak at noon, from which it decreases slowly in pitch and finally ends when the sun is gone from the sky. Originally, Keening was intense enough to be heard even by a vampire who lay in torpor and it made unlife for Kindred generally unbearable, driving many of the old Kindred who used to dwell there either insane or into other lands, away from its wail.<br /> Wards placed by the Hajj weakened the Keening - The Keening stopped only one time in its history, when Qarmatians, members of an Islamic sect, stole the Black Stone from the Kaaba in 950. This allowed Tarique to erect sorcerous wards that can contain a part of the Keening, although they cannot completely silence it.<br /> <b>Faith in Allah, however, seems to dampen the effect of the Keening</b>, so that many Ashirra are sincere in their devotion out of sheer fear. Many Ashirra are so accustomed to the sound of the Keening that they depend on it as a an alarm clock to awaken at dusk.<br /> <br /> The Ashirra have to be sincere even to live there... faith is part of their life, - sure you can fake it, but the Keening then would make very hard to even stay there<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}